   "Prices are listing prices at the retailers named, not transaction prices. Coverage is limited to retailers that allow automated collection, so this is not the whole market.",
   "The price shown is the cheapest new listing available online on the collection date.",
   "Amazon prices count only listings sold by Amazon.com or the part's own brand, and Best Buy prices only listings sold by Best Buy itself. Marketplace sellers are left out because their listings cannot be confirmed as new.",
   "A price backed by a single listing is marked low confidence: it is often one marketplace seller's asking price for a discontinued part.",
   "Score per dollar measures rendering throughput per dollar. It is a research lead, not buying advice.",
   "Blender Open Data is crowd-submitted: cooling, memory and drivers are not controlled.",
   "Scores come from a single Blender version and are never combined across versions.",
   "A fair price here means the price predicted from Blender rendering score alone. A part can cost more for reasons the benchmark does not measure, such as gaming performance, memory size or power draw.",
   "Graphics cards are scored on different Blender backends (OptiX, HIP, oneAPI), which favours NVIDIA cards, so AMD and Intel cards look more expensive for their score.",
   "The fit uses a few dozen parts. Gaps under the stated typical error are noise."
